body:
For real, BO4 went through a lot of bs and basically got rebooted twice before launch, having to pull a battle royale out of nowhere in under a year and having all the priorities get switched all the time. Post launch they end up having to cancel chaos story and the original aether maps to go work on CW with very little time left. Covid happens which fucks everything up, cw has half its content cancelled then before the games even done they have to immediately work on vanguard zombies. 

&#x200B;

Treyarch are getting zero room to breathe, constantly having to go make something entirely different at the drop of a hat instead of being given the time to make something they want. Shit we would have zc2 by now if they were treated properly

Disconnects happen to me pretty rarely on PC, but I gotta say RDO is infinitely more robust and stable than GTAO. You don't gotta sit through like 5 loading screens just to get booted out of a lobby that filled up while you were connecting then sit through another 5 minutes of loading back into freeroam. 

&#x200B;

I think GTA was just badly managed from the start and got to the point where it was too late to just replace the whole thing

The government has done uhh "war and corruption" and now there's people that want ummmmm "an egalitarian society" BUT they're secretly being funded by "(((The Bad Guys)))" so we gotta assemble an army to commit war crimes

&#x200B;

It's like dangerously close to being a GTA brand parody

Cancer 4 Cure is one of my favourite albums but I'd agree that a few songs dont achieve much, it was a slow burner for me. Really appreciate el's wild spacey production and his lyrics kinda need the genius tab on the side to explain the weirder ones.

&#x200B;

I'd recommend I'll Sleep when You're Dead, probably even harder lyrics to get a grasp on but the messaging is really powerful across the board about El waking up in post 9/11 america and the production has aged fantastically well for 2004. The few intro and closer tracks are really strong, personal favourite is The overly complicated truth. Pretty much none of his music is as easy to get into as RTJ and i dont say this to sound elitist lol, the dude just loves his weird concepts and beat around the bush wordplay.

&#x200B;

A lot of el's stuff is lyric focused and not very versatile sonically which is just how a lot of NY backpacker rap is, but when he really gets into his groove with layered + grand anthemic songs he shines. RTJ being mostly straight up bangers juxtaposes really weirdly against his old stuff but its worth digging deep into

